---
import RootLayout from "../../layouts/RootLayout.astro";
import RevealScript from "../../components/layout/RevealScript.astro";
import {ArrowRight} from "@lucide/astro/icons/index";
import {REGISTER_URL} from "../../consts";

const values = [
    {
        title: "Built by students",
        desc: "Studo comes from the same late-night study sessions you know. Every feature has to earn its place in a real exam week."
    },
    {
        title: "Your material first",
        desc: "Studo works from your own course material, not generic content. Your knowledge stays the source of truth."
    },
    {
        title: "Honest by default",
        desc: "The knowledge workspace stays free. You only pay when you want Sven to generate and do more of the work for you."
    },
];
---

<RootLayout
        title="About"
        description="Studo is built by and for students. Studo turns your own course material into a structured study system.">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 items-center justify-center">
        <section class="max-w-200 w-full flex flex-col justify-center pt-36 reveal-on-scroll gap-5 mb-10">
            <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-500 font-medium">About Studo</span>
            <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl font-medium">Built by and for students</h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-neutral-500">Studo started with a simple frustration: course
                material piles up, but knowing what to study next is hard. So we built one space that turns your
                material into a plan, practice and clear next steps.</p>

        </section>

        <hr class="border border-neutral-100">

        <section class="max-w-200 w-full flex flex-col justify-center reveal-on-scroll gap-5 mb-20">
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-medium">Where it started</h2>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-lg">
                Studo started as a way to survive one exam period. Slides in one folder,
                notes in another, a study plan that only existed in someone's head.
                The hard part was never finding material, it was knowing what still
                needed to be learned.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-lg">
                We're software engineering students ourselves, building Studo between
                our own lectures and deadlines. The first version was a small tool built
                to answer that one question during an exam week. It grew from there into
                a workspace built around the same material every study session already
                starts from: the course itself.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="max-w-200 w-full flex flex-col justify-center reveal-on-scroll gap-5 mb-20">
            <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-medium">Where we're going</h2>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-lg">
                Right now Studo turns your material into flashcards and a plan. The
                direction we're building toward is a workspace that understands your
                whole course, not just the parts you've already turned into a set,
                and can point you to what you haven't looked at yet.
            </p>
            <p class="text-neutral-500 text-lg">
                We're still students building this alongside our own exams, so every
                feature gets tested the same way you'd test it: under deadline
                pressure, the week before a real one.
            </p>
        </section>


        <RevealScript/>
    </div>
</RootLayout>
